 3045: /// [keepAlive] is true. Used to keep the caret block and selection endpoints
 3046: /// alive under editor virtualisation, so the caret and selection
 3047: /// highlight always paint and the geometry registry always knows their box.
 3048: ///
 3049: /// Also drives incremental rebuild: a block is only re-rendered when its
 3050: /// content changed ([blockChanged]) *or* when the selection / caret / IME
 3051: /// composition touches it. A pure caret move inside a different block leaves
 3052: /// this block's cached child intact, avoiding the inline-span rebuild that
 3053: /// would otherwise run for every block on every keystroke.
